msgstr "In spring the caterpillars come down the pine in procession, bury themselves a few centimetres deep and spin a cocoon. They spend months there as pupae, and some can even stay for a few years before coming out."

msgid "STORY_STAGE_MOTH_FACT"
msgstr "In summer, at night, the moths come out of the ground. They are grey, they do not eat and they live only a day or two. The females lay their eggs around two pine needles and cover them with scales from their bodies."

